      "nets": ["NET0023", "NET0050", "NET0017", "NET0055", "NET0006"],
      "observed": "The keyboard's COL1–COL5 lines are connected directly to SKW92A pins identified in the netlist as LAN_PORT1_TX+, LAN_PORT1_TX-, LAN_PORT1_RX+, LAN_PORT1_RX-, and LAN_PORT2_RX+.",
      "expected": "The specification says the keyboard matrix lines are wired to SKW92A GPIO pins. They should not share nets with the module's Ethernet PHY signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0023\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"COL1\")) (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_TX+\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0050\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"COL2\")) (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_TX-\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0017\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"10\") (pinfunction \"COL3\")) (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_RX+\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0055\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"17\") (pinfunction \"COL4\")) (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_RX-\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0006\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"COL5\")) (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT2_RX+\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "netlist shows 5 column + 7 row lines wired directly to SKW92A GPIO pins (matrix scanned by the module itself, not via an onboard keyboard controller)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The keyboard column lines are electrically tied to Ethernet PHY signals rather than the specified GPIOs. This is likely to prevent correct keyboard matrix scanning and can interfere with or damage Ethernet operation.",
      "confidence": 0.94
    }
  ],
  "summary": "An anomaly is present: all five keyboard column lines are connected to SKW92A pins identified as Ethernet PHY signals, contradicting the specified GPIO matrix interface."
}

